WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.500
Claimant: My 2023 fictional midsize sedan was parked overnight in a public lot. The next morning, I found a scratched door and a broken side window; the repair estimate is $1,400, I did not cause the damage, no authorized driver had the car, and a police report was filed.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.950
Adjuster: Is there any evidence that another person intentionally caused the damage?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:29.100
Claimant: I don’t know whether someone intentionally caused the damage; the facts only say that I did not cause it and no authorized driver had the car.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:49.250
Adjuster: Decision: needs_review. The damage is documented, but malicious damage by another person has not been established, and the policyholder or authorized-driver exclusion does not apply. Relevant clauses: AUTO-COMP-3, AUTO-COMP-4. Confidence: 0.98.
